		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=5508#p5508"><![CDATA[
Is there any reason why you don't encode the max endpoint flag inside your integer endpoint position? Like so,<div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>uint32_t ep= (uint32_t&amp;)p;uint32_t mask = -int32_t(ep &gt;&gt; 31) | 0x80000000;ep = ((ep ^ mask) &amp; 0xfffffffe) | (uint32_t)max;</code></pre></div>This does (sometimes) move the endpoints but is safe because min points are always &lt;= their true value and max points are always &gt;= their true value. In both cases the change in endpoint positions are only -1 or +1 respectively.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=148">John McCutchan</a> — Fri Sep 21, 2007 1:55 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
